It'd be easier to just say that cmevla is a morphological class of words
with its defining feature that it ends in  a consonant (there are other
features like fewer forbidden clusters compared to brivla).
One can of course add that cmevla don't have a place structure and are used
only for cmene. But that would be not for newbies but for those who is
already constructing words to add to JVS.

